WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Can you guys build on a budget,
with no bells and whistles?

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.120
Because people think we can't do that.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.680
Of course we can, but let's be honest.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.600
Nobody wants to build with
standardized materials.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.260
If I say, let's carpet the bedrooms
upstairs, it's like I said a four-letter

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.360
word. It's like, you know. The minute
you said carpet, that needs to be...

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.360
Nobody wants to see carpet. Now, this new
thing with these white oak floors, and

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.840
six- and seven-inch floors.
I mean, it's crazy numbers.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.620
When you start pricing out seven-inch
white oak floors, you can't even go with

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:32.080
real white oak anymore. The price is crazy.
So we go engineered. Even the

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.800
engineered is up in the $7, $8 range
for that, unfinished. You know, we

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.300
could definitely build on standard. You
just have to know, you've got to come clean

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.380
and tell us what you really want. And not
to say that once we start standard and

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.340
you want options, we'll put all the
options out there for you, and then it's up to

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.480
the client to decide. Yeah, I mean,
this is your standard Fabuwood kitchen, which is

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.500
middle of the line. You can go with a
builder's line, which we can make look just

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.060
as good. It's an import, but nobody, you
know, everybody tends to pull away from

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.020
the import line. Or you can go full
custom, where we custom build all your

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.380
cabinets, any wood species you want,
inset doors. But, you know, then you're

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.020
talking about increasing the budgets.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.040
You know, if you're a client looking to just
get some extra room, put your four

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.920
kids upstairs, get the five bedrooms,

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.820
you don't have to go nine-foot ceilings.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.360
You could just get that square footage
you want, keep everything down to a

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.760
minimum, and then you can always
add that stuff later, right?

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.140
That's right. That's right.
